{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01023",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 5.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "actually, doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.97,
      "end_seconds": 13.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Okay, you're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 17.5,
      "end_seconds": 23.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.19,
      "end_seconds": 33.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Well, I've been having skipped beats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.87,
      "end_seconds": 40.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "how long has it been like this? I ask because it helps me narrow things down"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.67,
      "end_seconds": 43.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Probably one week. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.37,
      "end_seconds": 46.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Does anything set it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.11,
      "end_seconds": 51.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "it's worse with lying down and caffeine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.32,
      "end_seconds": 60.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "Um, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 60.72,
      "end_seconds": 66.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.85,
      "end_seconds": 78.48,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, and a flutter in my chest. That's been about the same, about three months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 79.46,
      "end_seconds": 82.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "yes, exactly like that that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.82,
      "end_seconds": 85.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "What about dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.03,
      "end_seconds": 89.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 90.39,
      "end_seconds": 95.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "actually, doctor, I did notice dizziness. She doesn't always say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.89,
      "end_seconds": 103.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "no, I don't think I did maybe a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.05,
      "end_seconds": 114.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. A few quick ones: shortness of breath, chest pain or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.17,
      "end_seconds": 131.7,
      "duration_seconds": 15.53,
      "text": "Mm, no, no shortness of breath, no chest pain, no fainting. I did have being a bit anxious at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.52,
      "end_seconds": 137.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.92,
      "end_seconds": 140.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "nothing unusual, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.61,
      "end_seconds": 144.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Okay, has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.3,
      "end_seconds": 147.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.45,
      "end_seconds": 150.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.29,
      "end_seconds": 156.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "I had my septum straightened in my thirties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.27,
      "end_seconds": 161.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Okay, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.08,
      "end_seconds": 166.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 170.35,
      "end_seconds": 176.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "I'm not sure that's right. I seem to recall a problem with tramadol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.48,
      "end_seconds": 181.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "well, maybe, but I don't recall it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.67,
      "end_seconds": 196.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "alright, so that's unclear i'll record what each of you said any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.32,
      "end_seconds": 200.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.46,
      "end_seconds": 205.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.48,
      "end_seconds": 210.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "COPD, for five years. I have an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.26,
      "end_seconds": 217.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Alright, COPD and an irregular heartbeat, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.1,
      "end_seconds": 236.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.18,
      "end_seconds": 246.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "I'm on Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest i'm on metoprolol, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.05,
      "end_seconds": 253.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.26,
      "end_seconds": 260.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "50 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. Bisoprolol I don't take anymore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.78,
      "end_seconds": 265.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.16,
      "end_seconds": 283.01,
      "duration_seconds": 11.85,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I live with my elderly mother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.08,
      "end_seconds": 286.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.59,
      "end_seconds": 288.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.2,
      "end_seconds": 303.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.73,
      "end_seconds": 335.06,
      "duration_seconds": 26.33,
      "text": "all finished, thank you. Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably harmless extra heartbeats. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be an anxiety-related palpitation, so we'll keep that open. Just to be sure I understood. You've had skipped beats for one week, and no fainting or shortness of breath"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.88,
      "end_seconds": 339.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.82,
      "end_seconds": 351.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an ECG because of palpitations"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 353.35,
      "end_seconds": 356.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "the earliest is Monday, 3:30 pm"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.03,
      "end_seconds": 364.37,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "cut back on coffee and energy drinks and keep a a diary of when it happens"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.89,
      "end_seconds": 378.02,
      "duration_seconds": 13.13,
      "text": "Understood. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Come back if it carries on after a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.09,
      "end_seconds": 383.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.07,
      "end_seconds": 387.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "What are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.37,
      "end_seconds": 396.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "so, I come back if it carries on after a month is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.49,
      "end_seconds": 402.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "yes, exactly right. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.82,
      "end_seconds": 406.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.91,
      "end_seconds": 409.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}